{
  "video": {
    "id": "uBRdfsz_YB4",
    "title": "Transcription and Translation, excerpt 2 | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uBRdfsz_YB4",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 928,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 300,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 7.4,
      "end": 8.65,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Good morning."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 10.59,
      "end": 12.27,
      "duration": 1.68,
      "text": "Come on down."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 12.27,
      "end": 12.7,
      "duration": 0.43,
      "text": "All right."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 12.7,
      "end": 20.17,
      "duration": 7.47,
      "text": "So last time, we talked about the first couple of steps of"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 20.17,
      "end": 23.57,
      "duration": 3.4,
      "text": "the central dogma."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 23.57,
      "end": 33.2,
      "duration": 9.63,
      "text": "The central dogma is this name given to the statement DNA"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 33.2,
      "end": 35.26,
      "duration": 2.06,
      "text": "goes to DNA by replication."
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 40.32,
      "end": 46.016,
      "duration": 5.696,
      "text": "DNA goes to RNA by the process of transcription."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 50.09,
      "end": 52.44,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "We call it transcription because it's such a direct"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 52.44,
      "end": 56.02,
      "duration": 3.58,
      "text": "copying of letter to letter."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 56.02,
      "end": 61.3,
      "duration": 5.28,
      "text": "RNA goes to protein by a process of translation,"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 61.3,
      "end": 65.34,
      "duration": 4.04,
      "text": "because translation is the kind of word we would use"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 65.34,
      "end": 66.65,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "between two different languages."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 66.65,
      "end": 67.85,
      "duration": 1.2,
      "text": "And there are two different languages--"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 67.85,
      "end": 69.89,
      "duration": 2.04,
      "text": "the languages of nucleotides and the"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 69.89,
      "end": 72.88,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "language of amino acids."
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 72.88,
      "end": 76.36,
      "duration": 3.48,
      "text": "For what it's worth, it's name, the central dogma, goes"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 76.36,
      "end": 80.98,
      "duration": 4.62,
      "text": "back to Francis Crick, who called this the central dogma."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 80.98,
      "end": 83.7,
      "duration": 2.72,
      "text": "He did it in a kind of a light-hearted way, although"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 83.7,
      "end": 86.51,
      "duration": 2.81,
      "text": "others since then have criticized it, saying, oh,"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 86.51,
      "end": 88.19,
      "duration": 1.68,
      "text": "this is dogmatic."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 88.19,
      "end": 91.74,
      "duration": 3.55,
      "text": "Actually, Crick said not that DNA goes to"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 91.74,
      "end": 92.67,
      "duration": 0.93,
      "text": "RNA goes to the protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 92.67,
      "end": 96.19,
      "duration": 3.52,
      "text": "He says that all information flows from nucleic acids to"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 96.19,
      "end": 98.33,
      "duration": 2.14,
      "text": "proteins and not back again."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 98.33,
      "end": 100.75,
      "duration": 2.42,
      "text": "Because even then, Crick knew that in theory, there was no"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 100.75,
      "end": 103.74,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "reason you couldn't go back from RNA to DNA, and as we'll"
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 103.74,
      "end": 105.41,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "see today, that happens."
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 105.41,
      "end": 110.08,
      "duration": 4.67,
      "text": "So sometimes people say, oh, well, the central dogma was"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 110.08,
      "end": 112.48,
      "duration": 2.4,
      "text": "proved wrong because RNA can go back to DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 112.48,
      "end": 114.73,
      "duration": 2.25,
      "text": "Well, actually, that was even anticipated right then at the"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 114.73,
      "end": 116.645,
      "duration": 1.915,
      "text": "very beginning, when they realized RNA and DNA were"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 116.645,
      "end": 118.44,
      "duration": 1.795,
      "text": "essentially equivalent information."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 118.44,
      "end": 123.9,
      "duration": 5.46,
      "text": "The key step of converting nucleic acid information into"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 123.9,
      "end": 127.15,
      "duration": 3.25,
      "text": "protein information is translation."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 127.15,
      "end": 129.32,
      "duration": 2.17,
      "text": "And that's the last bit we have to fill in"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 129.32,
      "end": 131.05,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "and talk about today."
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 131.05,
      "end": 134.97,
      "duration": 3.92,
      "text": "So let me start by just reminding you-- because most"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 134.97,
      "end": 136.76,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "of you know it--"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 136.76,
      "end": 139.6,
      "duration": 2.84,
      "text": "how translation works."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 139.6,
      "end": 145.32,
      "duration": 5.72,
      "text": "So, in translation, you have a particular RNA that has been"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 145.32,
      "end": 148.86,
      "duration": 3.54,
      "text": "made by the cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 148.86,
      "end": 150.46,
      "duration": 1.6,
      "text": "Here's my RNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 150.46,
      "end": 153.54,
      "duration": 3.08,
      "text": "It goes five prime to three prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 153.54,
      "end": 155.79,
      "duration": 2.25,
      "text": "That's always the way we write these things."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 155.79,
      "end": 157.21,
      "duration": 1.42,
      "text": "And it has some particular sequence."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 157.21,
      "end": 158.81,
      "duration": 1.6,
      "text": "I'll make up a sequence here."
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 158.81,
      "end": 172.11,
      "duration": 13.3,
      "text": "A, U, A, C, G, A, U, G, A, A, G, A, G, G, C, C, C, dot dot"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 172.11,
      "end": 177.27,
      "duration": 5.16,
      "text": "dot, U, A, G, dot dot dot dot, three prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 177.27,
      "end": 179.14,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "All right."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 179.14,
      "end": 184.92,
      "duration": 5.78,
      "text": "Somehow, that's going to be translated into a protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 184.92,
      "end": 189.31,
      "duration": 4.39,
      "text": "It's translated according to a fantastic look-up up table."
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 189.31,
      "end": 193.75,
      "duration": 4.44,
      "text": "This look-up table is called the genetic code."
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 193.75,
      "end": 195.39,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "And the rule, the algorithm--"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 195.39,
      "end": 198.26,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "and it's a fairly simple algorithm, well, nothing's"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 198.26,
      "end": 201.94,
      "duration": 3.68,
      "text": "ever really simple in biology, but it's close to simple--"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 201.94,
      "end": 204.74,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "is you run along the sequence from the beginning."
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 204.74,
      "end": 205.82,
      "duration": 1.08,
      "text": "And you guys could write this."
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 205.82,
      "end": 208.2,
      "duration": 2.38,
      "text": "Anybody who's taken basic computer programming."
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 208.2,
      "end": 214.03,
      "duration": 5.83,
      "text": "Run along the sequence and find the first occurrence of"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 214.03,
      "end": 219.41,
      "duration": 5.38,
      "text": "A, U, G. Why A, U, G?"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 219.41,
      "end": 223.46,
      "duration": 4.05,
      "text": "Because A, U, G is the place you start."
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 223.46,
      "end": 226.68,
      "duration": 3.22,
      "text": "That's how life worked it out, and that's what it does."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 226.68,
      "end": 233.12,
      "duration": 6.44,
      "text": "After that, you parse the sequence in triplets."
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 233.12,
      "end": 238.665,
      "duration": 5.545,
      "text": "These triplets get the name codons."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 242.35,
      "end": 247.41,
      "duration": 5.06,
      "text": "And then you keep going until you hit one of"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 247.41,
      "end": 249.49,
      "duration": 2.08,
      "text": "three possible triplets."
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 249.49,
      "end": 256.56,
      "duration": 7.07,
      "text": "U, A, G. U, A, A. U, G, A. And you stop there."
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 259.93,
      "end": 263.35,
      "duration": 3.42,
      "text": "Any MIT student should be able to write an algorithm that"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 263.35,
      "end": 267.15,
      "duration": 3.8,
      "text": "takes a string, finds the first occurrence of U, A, G,"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 267.15,
      "end": 270.0,
      "duration": 2.85,
      "text": "breaks it up into triplets passed there, keeps going"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 270.0,
      "end": 274.01,
      "duration": 4.01,
      "text": "until you encounter one of these three triplets."
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 274.01,
      "end": 276.62,
      "duration": 2.61,
      "text": "What do you do for a given triplet?"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 276.62,
      "end": 278.66,
      "duration": 2.04,
      "text": "You look it up against the table."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 278.66,
      "end": 280.61,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "How many triplets are there?"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 280.61,
      "end": 284.55,
      "duration": 3.94,
      "text": "How many three-letter words are there with the four"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 284.55,
      "end": 287.128,
      "duration": 2.578,
      "text": "nucleotides?"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 287.128,
      "end": 287.57,
      "duration": 0.442,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: 64."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 287.57,
      "end": 288.39,
      "duration": 0.82,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: It's 4 to the 3rd--"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 288.39,
      "end": 290.6,
      "duration": 2.21,
      "text": "64 possible words."
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 290.6,
      "end": 294.8,
      "duration": 4.2,
      "text": "I've used up three of them to be stop, so there are 4 to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 294.8,
      "end": 299.36,
      "duration": 4.56,
      "text": "3rd possible codons."
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 299.36,
      "end": 301.92,
      "duration": 2.56,
      "text": "That's 64."
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 301.92,
      "end": 303.34,
      "duration": 1.42,
      "text": "Three stops."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 303.34,
      "end": 310.79,
      "duration": 7.45,
      "text": "The other 61 possible codons specify an amino acid."
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 310.79,
      "end": 310.89,
      "duration": 0.1,
      "text": "That's it."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 310.89,
      "end": 313.3,
      "duration": 2.41,
      "text": "There's a look-up table."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 313.3,
      "end": 314.67,
      "duration": 1.37,
      "text": "The genetic code."
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 314.67,
      "end": 317.43,
      "duration": 2.76,
      "text": "How many amino acids are there?"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 317.43,
      "end": 317.96,
      "duration": 0.53,
      "text": "20."
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 317.96,
      "end": 321.56,
      "duration": 3.6,
      "text": "And there are 61 possible codons, so that implies there"
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 321.56,
      "end": 323.78,
      "duration": 2.22,
      "text": "is some redundancy."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 323.78,
      "end": 326.0,
      "duration": 2.22,
      "text": "Some codons--"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 326.0,
      "end": 330.564,
      "duration": 4.564,
      "text": "some amino acids are coded for by the same codon."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 330.564,
      "end": 331.33,
      "duration": 0.766,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 331.33,
      "end": 332.2,
      "duration": 0.87,
      "text": "That's fine."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 332.2,
      "end": 335.3,
      "duration": 3.1,
      "text": "And in your book is the genetic code that is the"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 335.3,
      "end": 336.92,
      "duration": 1.62,
      "text": "look-up table here."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 336.92,
      "end": 352.07,
      "duration": 15.15,
      "text": "The genetic code translates these codons into amino acids."
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 352.07,
      "end": 354.87,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "Or to stop, in the case of the three stop signals."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 354.87,
      "end": 358.76,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "So for example, this A, U, G at the front is always"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 358.76,
      "end": 362.2,
      "duration": 3.44,
      "text": "translated into methionine."
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 362.2,
      "end": 363.56,
      "duration": 1.36,
      "text": "Met."
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 363.56,
      "end": 367.63,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "And if I've got it right, this should be a lysine."
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 367.63,
      "end": 368.13,
      "duration": 0.5,
      "text": "Here we go."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 368.13,
      "end": 374.83,
      "duration": 6.7,
      "text": "Arginine, proline, et cetera-- you just look it up."
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 374.83,
      "end": 375.58,
      "duration": 0.75,
      "text": "That's it."
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 375.58,
      "end": 378.29,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "That's the order in which you make the proteins."
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 378.29,
      "end": 381.31,
      "duration": 3.02,
      "text": "So you send off an order written in RNA, you send it"
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 381.31,
      "end": 383.63,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "off to the factory, the factory sends you back a"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 383.63,
      "end": 386.66,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "protein that is methionine, lysine, arginine, proline,"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 386.66,
      "end": 388.27,
      "duration": 1.61,
      "text": "blah, blah, blah, blah, blah."
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 388.27,
      "end": 390.76,
      "duration": 2.49,
      "text": "That's it."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 390.76,
      "end": 396.72,
      "duration": 5.96,
      "text": "This genetic code is essentially universal amongst"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 396.72,
      "end": 397.97,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "all of life."
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 402.183,
      "end": 403.9,
      "duration": 1.717,
      "text": "That's pretty stunning."
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 403.9,
      "end": 405.15,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "What does that tell you?"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 405.15,
      "end": 408.25,
      "duration": 3.1,
      "text": "The fact that all of life uses virtually the identical"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 408.25,
      "end": 409.1,
      "duration": 0.85,
      "text": "genetic code?"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 409.1,
      "end": 411.805,
      "duration": 2.705,
      "text": "There's actually a tiny difference between prokaryotes"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 411.805,
      "end": 415.13,
      "duration": 3.325,
      "text": "and eukaryotes affecting a codon and there's a tiny"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 415.13,
      "end": 416.29,
      "duration": 1.16,
      "text": "difference somewhere else."
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 416.29,
      "end": 419.56,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "But essentially, it's the exact same genetic code that"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 419.56,
      "end": 421.63,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "all of life uses."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 421.63,
      "end": 424.22,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "It's very unlikely that this genetic code is the only"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 424.22,
      "end": 427.99,
      "duration": 3.77,
      "text": "possible way you could make a genetic code, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 427.99,
      "end": 431.41,
      "duration": 3.42,
      "text": "So the fact that all of life uses, essentially, exactly the"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 431.41,
      "end": 435.45,
      "duration": 4.04,
      "text": "same code is pretty strong evidence that all currently"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 435.45,
      "end": 439.96,
      "duration": 4.51,
      "text": "existing life descends from a common ancestor."
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 439.96,
      "end": 443.54,
      "duration": 3.58,
      "text": "Because if these were evolved independently, it's extremely"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 443.54,
      "end": 446.08,
      "duration": 2.54,
      "text": "unlikely that you would have gotten exactly the same"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 446.08,
      "end": 447.56,
      "duration": 1.48,
      "text": "genetic code."
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 447.56,
      "end": 449.88,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "So that's an interesting point that you can see from just the"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 449.88,
      "end": 452.27,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "fact that everybody uses essentially the"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 452.27,
      "end": 454.45,
      "duration": 2.18,
      "text": "same genetic code."
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 454.45,
      "end": 458.04,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "It's a universal genetic code."
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 458.04,
      "end": 459.54,
      "duration": 1.5,
      "text": "All right."
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 459.54,
      "end": 465.16,
      "duration": 5.62,
      "text": "So I've expressed this to you in a completely computer"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 465.16,
      "end": 467.45,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "sciencey kind of way."
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 467.45,
      "end": 470.96,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "But, of course, the cell doesn't do this by computer"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 470.96,
      "end": 474.84,
      "duration": 3.88,
      "text": "science because cells are unable to write C code."
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 474.84,
      "end": 477.52,
      "duration": 2.68,
      "text": "The reason that cells are unable to write C code is C"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 477.52,
      "end": 481.71,
      "duration": 4.19,
      "text": "wasn't really developed until the last several decades, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 481.71,
      "end": 486.02,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "cells, pretty sure, precede the development of C code by"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 486.02,
      "end": 486.9,
      "duration": 0.88,
      "text": "Kernighan and Ritchie."
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 486.9,
      "end": 490.98,
      "duration": 4.08,
      "text": "So it's got to be the case that it's done some other way."
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 490.98,
      "end": 492.62,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "How is it done?"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 492.62,
      "end": 495.88,
      "duration": 3.26,
      "text": "Well, it's done like this."
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 495.88,
      "end": 497.75,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "And I'll just be very schematic and you'll"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 497.75,
      "end": 499.15,
      "duration": 1.4,
      "text": "get it in your book."
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 499.15,
      "end": 500.4,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "There's a big machine."
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 502.75,
      "end": 506.23,
      "duration": 3.48,
      "text": "The big machine here is called the ribosome."
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 511.59,
      "end": 515.86,
      "duration": 4.27,
      "text": "It consists, itself, of proteins and RNAs, and it's a"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 515.86,
      "end": 518.289,
      "duration": 2.429,
      "text": "huge structure."
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 518.289,
      "end": 522.23,
      "duration": 3.941,
      "text": "The huge structure needs to read codons."
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 525.0,
      "end": 526.72,
      "duration": 1.72,
      "text": "And this is a case where Francis Crick"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 526.72,
      "end": 528.5,
      "duration": 1.78,
      "text": "drove everybody nuts."
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 528.5,
      "end": 533.23,
      "duration": 4.73,
      "text": "Francis Crick, back in the 1950s, just sat at his desk"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 533.23,
      "end": 533.75,
      "duration": 0.52,
      "text": "and thought."
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 533.75,
      "end": 535.63,
      "duration": 1.88,
      "text": "He was terrible at doing experiments--"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 535.63,
      "end": 537.42,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "nobody really wanted to let him do experiments."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 537.42,
      "end": 539.83,
      "duration": 2.41,
      "text": "Francis was a great thinker."
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 539.83,
      "end": 540.31,
      "duration": 0.48,
      "text": "He thought."
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 540.31,
      "end": 545.21,
      "duration": 4.9,
      "text": "He said, golly, how can this sequence be translated into"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 545.21,
      "end": 546.56,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "amino acids?"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 546.56,
      "end": 548.88,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "Well, people at the time had all sorts of nutty ideas."
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 548.88,
      "end": 551.44,
      "duration": 2.56,
      "text": "Some of the nutty ideas was that the sequence of the RNA"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 551.44,
      "end": 554.84,
      "duration": 3.4,
      "text": "folded up into pockets that just fit a proline."
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 554.84,
      "end": 557.71,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "And another pocket that just an arginine."
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 557.71,
      "end": 560.04,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "And if you just think about the constraints to get that to"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 560.04,
      "end": 561.51,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "work, it's nuts."
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 561.51,
      "end": 564.84,
      "duration": 3.33,
      "text": "That the sequence itself would form perfect binding pockets"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 564.84,
      "end": 567.11,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "for the necessary amino acids."
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 567.11,
      "end": 569.36,
      "duration": 2.25,
      "text": "Crick said impossible."
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 569.36,
      "end": 572.35,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "He said the really sensible way to do this, if I were"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 572.35,
      "end": 575.1,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "running life, what I would do is I would"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 575.1,
      "end": 577.51,
      "duration": 2.41,
      "text": "have an adapter molecule."
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 577.51,
      "end": 581.34,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "The adapter molecule would be some kind of a nucleic acid,"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 581.34,
      "end": 585.96,
      "duration": 4.62,
      "text": "and the nucleic acid would kind of match the codon on one"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 585.96,
      "end": 592.02,
      "duration": 6.06,
      "text": "end and have the amino acid on the other end."
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 592.02,
      "end": 596.41,
      "duration": 4.39,
      "text": "And then there'd be another adapter, and the adapter would"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 596.41,
      "end": 599.64,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "have the next amino acid."
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 599.64,
      "end": 603.84,
      "duration": 4.2,
      "text": "And then you would catalyze a bond between them."
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 603.84,
      "end": 607.36,
      "duration": 3.52,
      "text": "Therefore, I predict, says Francis, there will be small"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 607.36,
      "end": 611.42,
      "duration": 4.06,
      "text": "adapter molecules, probably made out of RNAs themselves."
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 611.42,
      "end": 614.145,
      "duration": 2.725,
      "text": "And Francis called this the Adapter Hypothesis."
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 614.145,
      "end": 617.16,
      "duration": 3.015,
      "text": "It drove people crazy because, of course, he was right."
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 617.16,
      "end": 621.59,
      "duration": 4.43,
      "text": "People found the adapters and they would use transfer things"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 621.59,
      "end": 623.36,
      "duration": 1.77,
      "text": "that transfer information--"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 623.36,
      "end": 624.68,
      "duration": 1.32,
      "text": "get called transfer RNAs."
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 633.88,
      "end": 639.12,
      "duration": 5.24,
      "text": "What happens is the ribosome has pockets in which these"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 639.12,
      "end": 644.67,
      "duration": 5.55,
      "text": "transfer RNAs basically come in, match their sequence,"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 644.67,
      "end": 649.05,
      "duration": 4.38,
      "text": "there's a codon each of these transfer RNAs has a matching"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 649.05,
      "end": 652.06,
      "duration": 3.01,
      "text": "anticodon that matches the triplet, and it has already"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 652.06,
      "end": 654.38,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "attached to it an amino acid--"
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 654.38,
      "end": 657.64,
      "duration": 3.26,
      "text": "the right amino acid for that anticodon."
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 657.64,
      "end": 659.34,
      "duration": 1.7,
      "text": "How does that right amino acid get attached"
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 659.34,
      "end": 660.59,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "to the right tRNA?"
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 664.97,
      "end": 667.03,
      "duration": 2.06,
      "text": "There's an enzyme."
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 667.03,
      "end": 669.74,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "The job of that enzyme is to attach this amino acid,"
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 669.74,
      "end": 673.2,
      "duration": 3.46,
      "text": "proline, to this transfer RNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 673.2,
      "end": 676.87,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "It's a Prolyl-tRNA synthetase."
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 676.87,
      "end": 679.9,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "And its job is to put proline on the right tRNAs."
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 679.9,
      "end": 682.76,
      "duration": 2.86,
      "text": "There's another one that puts arginine on the right tRNAs."
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 682.76,
      "end": 685.03,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "There's a whole business that's set up to get the right"
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 685.03,
      "end": 687.92,
      "duration": 2.89,
      "text": "tRNAs, have the right amino acids attached to them through"
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 687.92,
      "end": 690.22,
      "duration": 2.3,
      "text": "a bunch of enzymes floating around."
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 690.22,
      "end": 694.332,
      "duration": 4.112,
      "text": "So then these tRNAs with the amino acid attached drop in,"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 694.332,
      "end": 697.91,
      "duration": 3.578,
      "text": "they drop into the next position, and a bond--"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 697.91,
      "end": 701.41,
      "duration": 3.5,
      "text": "the peptide bond-- is catalyzed."
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 701.41,
      "end": 702.66,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Interesting factoid."
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 705.73,
      "end": 710.01,
      "duration": 4.28,
      "text": "The catalysis, this enzymatic catalysis to join together"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 710.01,
      "end": 713.02,
      "duration": 3.01,
      "text": "those amino acids is actually carried out not by the"
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 713.02,
      "end": 715.9,
      "duration": 2.88,
      "text": "proteins in a ribosome, but actually"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 715.9,
      "end": 717.86,
      "duration": 1.96,
      "text": "by RNA in the ribosome."
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 717.86,
      "end": 721.122,
      "duration": 3.262,
      "text": "The RNA is the enzyme."
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 721.122,
      "end": 722.81,
      "duration": 1.688,
      "text": "You know why that's kind of cool?"
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 725.37,
      "end": 728.05,
      "duration": 2.68,
      "text": "If this bothers you, just forget it, but one of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 728.05,
      "end": 730.72,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "mysteries about how you ever go from DNA to RNA to protein"
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 730.72,
      "end": 733.57,
      "duration": 2.85,
      "text": "and all of that is how the whole thing ever got started."
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 733.57,
      "end": 735.93,
      "duration": 2.36,
      "text": "How could you possibly have gotten protein synthesis"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 735.93,
      "end": 739.98,
      "duration": 4.05,
      "text": "started if the things that were needed to make protein"
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 739.98,
      "end": 741.23,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "synthesis were proteins?"
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 744.2,
      "end": 748.72,
      "duration": 4.52,
      "text": "So this is actually an echo of an ancient world 3 billion"
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 748.72,
      "end": 753.72,
      "duration": 5.0,
      "text": "years ago, where this was all probably carried out by RNAs."
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 753.72,
      "end": 757.48,
      "duration": 3.76,
      "text": "RNA was probably the early catalysts for most things, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 757.48,
      "end": 760.7,
      "duration": 3.22,
      "text": "we still see evidence of the fact that even today your"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 760.7,
      "end": 764.11,
      "duration": 3.41,
      "text": "peptide bonds are catalyzed actually by RNA and they're"
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 764.11,
      "end": 766.26,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "doing the enzymatic work."
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 766.26,
      "end": 767.63,
      "duration": 1.37,
      "text": "Anyway, it's kind of cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 230,
      "start": 767.63,
      "end": 769.23,
      "duration": 1.6,
      "text": "If you didn't get that, don't worry about it, but"
    },
    {
      "index": 231,
      "start": 769.23,
      "end": 770.12,
      "duration": 0.89,
      "text": "it's kind of cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 232,
      "start": 770.12,
      "end": 771.41,
      "duration": 1.29,
      "text": "So then what happens after you attach the"
    },
    {
      "index": 233,
      "start": 771.41,
      "end": 772.84,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "first two amino acids?"
    },
    {
      "index": 234,
      "start": 772.84,
      "end": 777.32,
      "duration": 4.48,
      "text": "Well, the ribosome chugs down here and grabs the next code--"
    },
    {
      "index": 235,
      "start": 777.32,
      "end": 778.32,
      "duration": 1.0,
      "text": "these two shift over."
    },
    {
      "index": 236,
      "start": 778.32,
      "end": 780.21,
      "duration": 1.89,
      "text": "You can either think about the ribosome moving this way or"
    },
    {
      "index": 237,
      "start": 780.21,
      "end": 781.68,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "the RNA moving that way."
    },
    {
      "index": 238,
      "start": 781.68,
      "end": 784.83,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "The next tRNA drops in, the next bond gets made, chugs"
    },
    {
      "index": 239,
      "start": 784.83,
      "end": 787.92,
      "duration": 3.09,
      "text": "over, the next one drops in, the next one gets made, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 240,
      "start": 787.92,
      "end": 790.86,
      "duration": 2.94,
      "text": "onward like that until it hits a stop codon at which, it"
    },
    {
      "index": 241,
      "start": 790.86,
      "end": 792.83,
      "duration": 1.97,
      "text": "releases it."
    },
    {
      "index": 242,
      "start": 792.83,
      "end": 794.26,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "The ribosome knows to release it."
    },
    {
      "index": 243,
      "start": 794.26,
      "end": 795.9,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "There's actually a little factor that drops in and tells"
    },
    {
      "index": 244,
      "start": 795.9,
      "end": 797.12,
      "duration": 1.22,
      "text": "it to release it there."
    },
    {
      "index": 245,
      "start": 797.12,
      "end": 798.8,
      "duration": 1.68,
      "text": "And that's how you make proteins--"
    },
    {
      "index": 246,
      "start": 798.8,
      "end": 799.73,
      "duration": 0.93,
      "text": "kind of cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 247,
      "start": 799.73,
      "end": 801.345,
      "duration": 1.615,
      "text": "It works very well."
    },
    {
      "index": 248,
      "start": 801.345,
      "end": 803.2,
      "duration": 1.855,
      "text": "It chugs along in that fashion."
    },
    {
      "index": 249,
      "start": 803.2,
      "end": 806.56,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "For you computer scientists, what you basically have is a"
    },
    {
      "index": 250,
      "start": 806.56,
      "end": 807.99,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "two-tape turing machine--"
    },
    {
      "index": 251,
      "start": 807.99,
      "end": 810.51,
      "duration": 2.52,
      "text": "you're reading one tape and writing to the other tape."
    },
    {
      "index": 252,
      "start": 810.51,
      "end": 812.1,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "There's a nucleic acid tape and there's"
    },
    {
      "index": 253,
      "start": 812.1,
      "end": 813.6,
      "duration": 1.5,
      "text": "an amino acid tape."
    },
    {
      "index": 254,
      "start": 813.6,
      "end": 816.29,
      "duration": 2.69,
      "text": "If you're not a computer scientist, forget I said that."
    },
    {
      "index": 255,
      "start": 816.29,
      "end": 817.08,
      "duration": 0.79,
      "text": "OK."
    },
    {
      "index": 256,
      "start": 817.08,
      "end": 821.42,
      "duration": 4.34,
      "text": "So it's basically a two-tape tape turing machine where the"
    },
    {
      "index": 257,
      "start": 821.42,
      "end": 825.37,
      "duration": 3.95,
      "text": "RNA is coming through here and the protein is coming out that"
    },
    {
      "index": 258,
      "start": 825.37,
      "end": 828.31,
      "duration": 2.94,
      "text": "way, but the amino acids attach to each other"
    },
    {
      "index": 259,
      "start": 828.31,
      "end": 831.22,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "until it comes off."
    },
    {
      "index": 260,
      "start": 831.22,
      "end": 834.11,
      "duration": 2.89,
      "text": "In fact, actually, very recently, a Nobel Prize was"
    },
    {
      "index": 261,
      "start": 834.11,
      "end": 837.77,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "awarded last year for beautiful, beautiful work on"
    },
    {
      "index": 262,
      "start": 837.77,
      "end": 841.03,
      "duration": 3.26,
      "text": "how this actually takes place-- the molecular details"
    },
    {
      "index": 263,
      "start": 841.03,
      "end": 842.78,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "of the ribosome."
    },
    {
      "index": 264,
      "start": 842.78,
      "end": 844.6,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "Really gorgeous."
    },
    {
      "index": 265,
      "start": 844.6,
      "end": 847.694,
      "duration": 3.094,
      "text": "Any questions about that?"
    },
    {
      "index": 266,
      "start": 847.694,
      "end": 849.152,
      "duration": 1.458,
      "text": "Yeah."
    },
    {
      "index": 267,
      "start": 849.152,
      "end": 850.61,
      "duration": 1.458,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Is that not susceptible to the same error"
    },
    {
      "index": 268,
      "start": 850.61,
      "end": 852.56,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "as replication is?"
    },
    {
      "index": 269,
      "start": 852.56,
      "end": 855.26,
      "duration": 2.7,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Oh, is that not susceptible to the same error?"
    },
    {
      "index": 270,
      "start": 858.25,
      "end": 859.87,
      "duration": 1.62,
      "text": "Does the ribosome ever make mistakes?"
    },
    {
      "index": 271,
      "start": 862.5,
      "end": 864.74,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "It does."
    },
    {
      "index": 272,
      "start": 864.74,
      "end": 868.342,
      "duration": 3.602,
      "text": "What happens if you make the wrong protein?"
    },
    {
      "index": 273,
      "start": 868.342,
      "end": 870.14,
      "duration": 1.798,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]."
    },
    {
      "index": 274,
      "start": 870.14,
      "end": 871.44,
      "duration": 1.3,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Oh well."
    },
    {
      "index": 275,
      "start": 871.44,
      "end": 874.89,
      "duration": 3.45,
      "text": "The answer turns out to be \"oh well\" because for any given"
    },
    {
      "index": 276,
      "start": 874.89,
      "end": 877.18,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "DNA, you make lots of RNAs."
    },
    {
      "index": 277,
      "start": 877.18,
      "end": 879.335,
      "duration": 2.155,
      "text": "For any RNA, you use it again and again to"
    },
    {
      "index": 278,
      "start": 879.335,
      "end": 880.81,
      "duration": 1.475,
      "text": "make lots of proteins."
    },
    {
      "index": 279,
      "start": 880.81,
      "end": 883.67,
      "duration": 2.86,
      "text": "And if the occasional protein is not so good, if the quality"
    },
    {
      "index": 280,
      "start": 883.67,
      "end": 887.66,
      "duration": 3.99,
      "text": "control is not perfect, it's much less serious than if your"
    },
    {
      "index": 281,
      "start": 887.66,
      "end": 890.82,
      "duration": 3.16,
      "text": "master instructions in the DNA were not perfect."
    },
    {
      "index": 282,
      "start": 890.82,
      "end": 892.55,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "So the cell actually devotes a lot less"
    },
    {
      "index": 283,
      "start": 892.55,
      "end": 894.36,
      "duration": 1.81,
      "text": "attention to quality control."
    },
    {
      "index": 284,
      "start": 894.36,
      "end": 894.55,
      "duration": 0.19,
      "text": "Now."
    },
    {
      "index": 285,
      "start": 894.55,
      "end": 896.57,
      "duration": 2.02,
      "text": "That's not to say there isn't important quality control."
    },
    {
      "index": 286,
      "start": 896.57,
      "end": 898.85,
      "duration": 2.28,
      "text": "There are quality control mechanisms, but it doesn't"
    },
    {
      "index": 287,
      "start": 898.85,
      "end": 901.84,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "have to be as accurate as one error in a billion, like you"
    },
    {
      "index": 288,
      "start": 901.84,
      "end": 903.81,
      "duration": 1.97,
      "text": "want to be in copying your DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 289,
      "start": 903.81,
      "end": 906.91,
      "duration": 3.1,
      "text": "And that's really an important point, is the archival copy"
    },
    {
      "index": 290,
      "start": 906.91,
      "end": 910.58,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "has to be really good, but little yellow sticky notes--"
    },
    {
      "index": 291,
      "start": 910.58,
      "end": 912.52,
      "duration": 1.94,
      "text": "what you make from it, which are basically RNA or the"
    },
    {
      "index": 292,
      "start": 912.52,
      "end": 914.81,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "little yellow sticky notes you copied down-- they don't have"
    },
    {
      "index": 293,
      "start": 914.81,
      "end": 915.43,
      "duration": 0.62,
      "text": "to be perfect."
    },
    {
      "index": 294,
      "start": 915.43,
      "end": 917.33,
      "duration": 1.9,
      "text": "And each copy, the protein doesn't have to be--"
    },
    {
      "index": 295,
      "start": 917.33,
      "end": 919.75,
      "duration": 2.42,
      "text": "and if the protein is not perfect, there are mechanisms"
    },
    {
      "index": 296,
      "start": 919.75,
      "end": 922.54,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "that take unfolded proteins and degrade them."
    },
    {
      "index": 297,
      "start": 922.54,
      "end": 926.04,
      "duration": 3.5,
      "text": "So it turns out there are ways to achieve quality control in"
    },
    {
      "index": 298,
      "start": 926.04,
      "end": 926.61,
      "duration": 0.57,
      "text": "that sense."
    },
    {
      "index": 299,
      "start": 926.61,
      "end": 927.86,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "It's a great question."
    }
  ],
